Head of HR & Operations Manager
Robert Walters
Brussels, Belgium
Are you an experienced Head of HR & Operations Manager looking for a strategic leadership role in HR, Operations, People Management and Business Operations? This exciting opportunity in Brussels within a leading international public affairs consultancy offers the chance to combine HR leadership, operational management and business excellence in one impactful position. As Head of HR & Operations Manager, you will play a key role in strengthening HR processes, optimising business operations, supporting senior leadership and driving organisational performance in a dynamic, international and collaborative environment. If you enjoy combining strategic thinking with hands-on execution this could be your next career move.
Your responsibilities as Head of HR & Operations Manager
As Head of HR & Operations Manager, you will be responsible for both the strategic and operational aspects of the organisation.
Oversee HR administration, payroll, benefits, employment contracts and compliance with Belgian employment legislation;
Manage onboarding, offboarding, employee policies and internal HR procedures;
Act as a trusted HR partner for employee relations, workplace concerns and confidential HR matters;
Support employee engagement through internal communication, wellbeing initiatives and team activities;
Coordinate recruitment processes, talent development initiatives, performance review cycles and training programmes;
Ensure smooth office operations by managing facilities, suppliers, procurement and workplace services;
Monitor operational compliance, governance processes and expense management;
Lead and support administrative, reception and IT support teams to ensure efficient daily operations;
Oversee business travel arrangements, meetings, corporate events and internal activities;
Continuously improve operational processes, digital tools and document management systems to increase efficiency and support business growth.
About you
To succeed as Head of HR & Operations Manager, you bring a strong combination of HR expertise, operations management and leadership experience.
You have significant experience in HR management and business operations in Belgium;
You have a strong understanding of Belgian employment law and HR compliance requirements;
You have experience managing operational processes, administration, suppliers and support teams;
You are highly organised, structured and able to manage multiple priorities effectively;
You combine strategic thinking with a practical and hands-on mindset;
You have strong communication skills and build trusted relationships with stakeholders at all levels;
You are a proactive problem solver with strong decision-making and project management abilities;
You demonstrate a high level of integrity, discretion and professionalism;
Fluency in English and Dutch is required. Knowledge of French is a plus;
You are motivated by continuous improvement and delivering operational excellence.
What we offer
As Head of HR & Operations Manager, you will benefit from:
A strategic leadership role within a leading international public affairs consultancy;
The opportunity to shape HR processes, operational structures and workplace culture;
A highly visible position working closely with senior leadership and key stakeholders;
The autonomy to improve processes and contribute to organisational growth;
A varied leadership role combining HR management, operations management, people leadership and strategic initiatives;
A competitive salary package with attractive benefits.
Apply for this Head of HR & Operations Manager opportunity
This is a unique opportunity for an experienced Head of HR & Operations Manager, HR Manager, Operations Manager or People & Operations Leader who wants to combine HR expertise with operational leadership and make a tangible impact on an organisation's success.
In this strategic leadership role, you will create efficient HR and operational processes, support employees throughout the organization and partner with senior leadership to drive sustainable business growth.
Apply today and take the opportunity to shape the future of a leading international public affairs consultancy in Brussels.
Robert Walters Belgium is acting as an Employment Agency in relation to this vacancy.
Apply Now
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.

Advocacy Adviser, Europe
Center for Reproductive Rights
Brussels or Remote
Department:
Global Advocacy and Regional Programs, Europe
Center Background:
The Center for Reproductive Rights is a global human rights organization working to ensure that reproductive rights are protected in law as fundamental human rights worldwide. With offices in New York City, and Washington, D.C.; Nairobi, Kenya; Bogota, Colombia; and Geneva, Switzerland, the Center is a non-profit, non-partisan organization changing law and policy throughout Africa, Asia, Europe, Latin America and the Caribbean, and the United States. Our 270+ diverse professionals are committed to advancing the Center’s human rights mission through game-changing litigation, legal policy, and advocacy work. This has powered the Center’s exceptional growth to an operating budget of over $60 million and won the respect of law firms in countries around the world. Our global pro bono network includes over
3,000
lawyers across
6
continents,
88
countries, and
140+
law firms. Last year, law firms contributed over
$35 million USD
in pro bono legal services. The Center’s Strategic Plan sets a high mark for impact: By 2030, half of the world’s population will be living under stronger protections for reproductive rights than they were in 2020. The Center has a record of success to back up this ambitious goal. Since our founding in 1992, the Center has transformed how reproductive rights are understood and applied by courts, governments, and human rights bodies worldwide on issues including maternal health, abortion, assisted reproduction, and adolescent sexual and reproductive health and rights. We have won groundbreaking cases before national courts, U.N. Committees, and regional human rights bodies. The Center has also led development of historic, proactive legislation advancing robust protections for reproductive rights. It has built the legal capacity of women’s rights advocates in more than 65 countries and counting. To learn more about the Center, please go to
www.reproductiverights.org
.
The Job:
Reporting to the Associate Director for National Legal Strategies, Europe, the Advocacy Adviser is responsible for developing and implementing advocacy strategies to advance and protect reproductive rights in Europe, particularly in Central and Eastern Europe, and works closely with other Europe program staff to ensure alignment with the regional Work Plan and the Center’s Strategic Plan.
This position will be based remotely in Germany, Poland, Romania, or Brussels (Belgium)
.
Primary Responsibilities:
Support development and implementation of advocacy, litigation and communication strategies and activities at national, regional, and international levels as relevant to advancing legal and policy reform on thematic reproductive rights priorities and defending against regression in relevant focus countries, in particular in Central and Eastern Europe;
Monitor legal and policy developments on sexual and reproductive rights issues in Europe, with particular focus on Central and Eastern Europe;
Undertake legal and policy research and analysis of national laws and policies and international human rights law and standards to inform advocacy priorities;
Develop and strengthen national-level partnerships with civil society organizations, policy makers and other key stakeholders in agreed focus countries;
Deliver high quality programmatic outputs for regional, country, and thematic priorities, including drafting advocacy materials, submissions, briefing notes, and other written outputs on a variety of sexual and reproductive rights issues;
Design and deliver presentations, training modules and capacity building initiatives;
Organize convenings, workshops, and other events and assist with preparation of presentations for conferences and meetings;
Represent the Center externally on matters related to reproductive rights in Europe through public speaking and engagement with media;
Partner with the Associate Director for National Legal Strategies to develop and implement the regional Work Plan in accordance with the Strategic Plan, and support other institutional processes as requested;
Support fundraising strategies, including through research and drafting materials, as requested;
Regional travel is required.
Compensation:
The Center offers a competitive salary commensurate with experience.
Commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion:
The Center is committed to inclusive hiring and dedicated to diversity in our work and staff. We strongly encourage people from all communities to apply. If you are excited about this role but unsure about whether your experience aligns with the job description, we encourage you to apply. You may be the right candidate for this or other roles. To learn more about the Center’s commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion, please visit
Diversity, Equity and Inclusion | Center for Reproductive Rights
.
Requirements:
Master’s degree in law, human rights, political science, public policy or a related field;
Minimum of 8 years of work experience in sexual and reproductive health and rights, gender equality, human rights, or related social justice field;
Strong background in international and European human rights law, standards, and systems. Experience in conducting advocacy before international and regional human rights mechanisms or with EU institutions and processes desirable;
Experience in national level advocacy and legal or policy reform strategies in Europe, particularly in Central and Eastern Europe, and in collaborating and partnering with NGOs and other civil society actors to achieve social justice goals;
Strong commitment to the Center’s mission, purpose, and values;
Fluency in written and spoken English and at least one other European language, ideally a language from Central or Eastern Europe;
Excellent oral and written communication skills, including drafting and editing;
Strong research and analytical skills and ability to process complex information;
Strong critical thinking skills and creative approach;
Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively;
Excellent organizational and time management skills, including ability to self-motivate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, work under pressure and meet tight deadlines;
Ability to work in a multicultural, diverse, and performance-driven environment;
Ability to travel for work.
Apply Now
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.

Referent/in/(Junior) Manager/in Stoffregulierung und Nachhaltigkeit Elektro-Hausgeräte/Home Appliances (w/m/d)
ZVEI - Zentralverband der Elektro- und Digitalindustrie
Frankfurt am Main, Berlin or Brussels
Der ZVEI ist der Verband der Elektro- und Digitalindustrie. Als Teil unseres dynamischen ZVEI-Teams und gemeinsam mit unseren mehr als 1.100 Mitgliedsunternehmen und 170 Kolleginnen und Kollegen gestalten Sie aktiv die Zukunft mit Ihren "Electrifying Ideas" und profitieren dabei von einem breiten Netzwerk in einer der innovativsten Branchen Deutschlands. Nutzen Sie die Möglichkeit, Ihre Expertise in zukunftsweisenden Technologien einzubringen. Bei uns erwartet Sie eine offene Unternehmenskultur mit flachen Hierarchien, die Raum für Ihre persönliche und berufliche Entwicklung bietet. Werden Sie Teil unseres engagierten Teams, das die digitale und nachhaltige Transformation vorantreibt.
Wir suchen zum nächstmöglichen Zeitpunkt Verstärkung für unser engagiertes Team im ZVEI e. V. am Standort
Frankfurt am Main, Berlin oder Brüssel
. Sie möchten Zukunftsthemen der Consumer-Technologien, insbesondere der Elektro-Hausgerätebranche aktiv mitgestalten? Dann erwartet Sie bei uns ein spannendes Umfeld zwischen Technik, Nachhaltigkeit und europäischer Regulierung. Stoffregulierung, Ökodesign und weitere Umweltanforderungen verändern die Anforderungen an Produkte und Unternehmen spürbar. In dieser Position bringen Sie Ihre Expertise ein, analysieren politische und regulatorische Entwicklungen und vertreten die Interessen einer innovativen Branche, die den Wandel hin zu mehr Nachhaltigkeit aktiv vorantreibt.
Ihre Aufgaben
Vertretung der gemeinsamen Interessen unserer Mitglieder der Elektro-Hausgeräteindustrie gegenüber Behörden sowie umweltpolitischen Entscheidenden in Deutschland und der Europäischen Union;
Monitoring und Analyse von regulatorischen Entwicklungen sowie Stakeholdern im Bereich der Stoffregulierung, des Ökodesign sowie anderer Umweltthemen für Elektro-Hausgeräte;
Erarbeitung und Abstimmung von Positionen zu regulatorischen und produktbezogenen Anforderungen im engen Austausch mit Vertreterinnen und Vertretern der Elektro-Hausgeräteindustrie in Deutschland;
Moderation von Expertengremien zu technischen und regulatorischen Fragestellungen sowie Förderung des Meinungs- und Erfahrungsaustauschs;
Weiterentwicklung der bestehenden Themenfelder sowie Identifikation und Bewertung neuer regulatorischer Entwicklungen;
Vertretung des ZVEI in Branchenverbänden, insbesondere dem europäischen Dachverband APPLiA, Mitwirkung in den entsprechenden Gremien und Umsetzung relevanter europäischer Branchenpositionen in Deutschland.
Ihr Profil
Erfolgreich abgeschlossenes Hochschulstudium, vorzugsweise in den Ingenieurwissenschaften oder in einem naturwissen-schaftlichen Fach, idealerweise mit Schwerpunkt Chemie; Bewerberinnen und Bewerber aus den Politik-, Kommunikations- oder Rechtswissenschaften sind bei entsprechender technischer Affinität ebenfalls willkommen;
Ausgeprägte kommunikative und analytische Fähigkeiten, verbunden mit hoher Organisationsstärke und Teamorientierung;
Ausgeprägtes Interesse an technischen und regulatorischen Zusammenhängen;
Eigeninitiative, Flexibilität und Reisebereitschaft;
Fähigkeit, komplexe Sachverhalte strukturiert aufzubereiten und adressatengerecht zu kommunizieren sowie sicher gegenüber Dritten zu vertreten;
Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift.
Unser Angebot
Zuschuss zur betrieblichen Altersversorgung;
30 Tage Urlaub + zusätzlich betriebsfrei zwischen 24.12 – 31.12;
Gleitzeit & Möglichkeit zum mobilen Arbeiten;
Vermögenswirksame Leistungen;
Betriebliche Unfallversicherung;
Je nach Standort unterschiedliche Zuschüsse zur Mobilität;
Kantinenzuschuss (Standort Frankfurt) bzw. Pluxee Gutscheine (Standort Berlin/Brüssel);
BUK Familienservice;
Kostenfreie Getränke (Kaffee & Wasser);
... und einiges mehr.
Haben wir Ihr Interesse geweckt?
Dann freuen wir uns auf Ihre aussagekräftige Bewerbung inkl. Zeugnissen, Gehaltsvorstellung und frühestmöglichem Eintrittstermin.
Mehr Informationen über den ZVEI unter
www.zvei.org
.
Mehr Informationen zu unserer Datenschutzerklärung unter
www.zvei.org/datenschutz
.
ZVEI e. V.
Verband der Elektro- und Digitalindustrie
Amelia-Mary-Earhart-Str. 12 60549 Frankfurt am Main
Telefon:
+49 69 6302-0
Fax: +49 69 6302-269
E-Mail:
personal@zvei.org
,
www.zvei.org
Apply Now
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
