PR/Communications Officer
BIR - Bureau of International Recycling
Brussels, Belgium
The Bureau of International Recycling, the global federation of recycling industries, is
searching for an experienced multilingual PR/Communications Officer to join its communications department. In this role, you will play a key part in amplifying our voice and promoting the critical role of recycling in a circular economy.
BIR counts over 1100 corporate members and national associations in 73 countries. Together, these members form the largest international recycling federation. The organisation covers eight material streams – iron/steel, non-ferrous metals, paper, textiles, stainless steel/special alloys, plastics, tyres/rubber and electrics/electronics/EV batteries. BIR is a non-profit organisation under Belgian law (AISBL), with its registered office headquartered in Brussels, Belgium. The BIR Secretariat is composed of a small but efficient team of 13 professionals from diverse backgrounds and nationalities.
Responsibilities of the position:
Contribute to the development and production of BIR publications, including magazines, reports and newsletters;
Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to develop engaging web content and communication tools;
Enhance BIR's visual identity through the creation of compelling graphics and presentations;
Support with media relations and outreach activities to raise awareness of BIR and its initiatives;
Assist the social media manager with campaigns and online presence optimization;
Attend BIR’s twice-yearly recycling conventions.
Qualifications:
Bachelor's degree in communications, public relations, journalism or a related field;
Previous experience in a PR/communications role (minimum 2-3 years) a must;
Solid experience with digital communication platforms (content creation, photo editing, digital marketing, website management);
Track record in managing publications and other communication materials;
Excellent writing and editing skills in English (C1);
Proficiency in French is a significant advantage, and fluency in additional European languages is a plus.
Benefits:
The opportunity to work for a leading international organisation in the field of sustainable resource management;
A dynamic, multicultural and collaborative work environment;
Competitive salary and benefits package.
To apply:
Send your CV and motivation letter (one page max., non AI-generated, including your net salary expectations) before Friday,
18 September 2026
to Elisabeth Christ, BIR Communications Director at
jobs.communications@bir.org
.
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
Share this Job

Junior Institutional Relations Officer
(CIP or Intern)
IOGP - International Association of Oil & Gas Producers
Brussels, Belgium
€ 1,700 per month net
Position summary:
We are recruiting a passionate, organized, and meticulous full-time junior institutional relations officer to join our Institutional relations team and provide comprehensive support in a variety of tasks related to administration, outreach and advocacy.
Scope, main purpose & objectives:
Assist with the preparation of briefing packs, meeting materials and background documents; take notes and follow up on action points;
Provide day-to-day administrative support to the Institutional Relations team, including preparing and updating PowerPoint presentations, Excel trackers, contact lists and internal documents;
Support meeting and travel arrangements, including scheduling, registrations, bookings, agendas and practical logistics;
Maintain and update stakeholder databases, mailing lists, meeting records and institutional contact information;
Support the organisation of meetings, events and institutional visits, including invitations, participant tracking and logistics;
Monitor selected EU institutional and legislative developments and provide short internal updates;
Conduct stakeholder mapping and research on EU institutions, Member States and relevant third countries;
Support engagement with the European Parliament, European Commission and Council, including coordination with MEP offices and other institutional contacts;
Contribute, under the guidance of the Institutional Relations team, to IOGP Europe’s outreach and advocacy activities.
Qualifications & experience:
Proficient in database management and Microsoft 365, with strong skills in Excel, PowerPoint, and Outlook;
Fluent in English and strong knowledge of at least one other European language;
License and/or Master’s Degree in European or Public Affairs, Political Science, International Relations or equivalent;
Outcome-driven and solution-oriented attitude;
Adaptable, comfortable working in a very fast-paced environment and able to re-prioritize on the go;
Ability to run multiple projects simultaneously;
Good understanding of EU policymaking dynamics and processes;
Ability to contribute innovative ideas regarding the outreach to the EU Institutions;
Solid research, analytical and IT;
Experience in EU Public Affairs, including traineeship/Blue books in the European institutions or in other trade associations is a plus.
Knowledge & attributes:
Proactive mindset, capable of identifying and resolving potential challenges before they escalate, while diplomatically managing complex situations;
Strong team spirit, working in solidarity, and a collegial approach to decision-making;
Ability to help overcome differences and reach a compromise;
Strong communication skills;
Apply a solution oriented mindset in stressful and uncertain situations;
Good knowledge of sustainability, energy, and climate issues; familiarity with the oil & gas industry is an advantage;
Open to travel and flexibility to occasionally work outside regular office hours.
Apply Now
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
Share this Job

Public Affairs Manager (Tech Policy)
SAMMAN Law & Corporate Affairs
Brussels, Belgium
Join a leading boutique tech policy and government affairs consultancy
SAMMAN Law & Corporate Affairs is looking for a Public Affairs Manager to join our Brussels team and contribute to shaping some of the most important policy debates impacting the digital economy in Europe.
Who we are
SAMMAN Law & Corporate Affairs is a leading law firm and consultancy specialized in public policy, government affairs, and strategic advocacy at both the French and European Union levels.
Recognized for our expertise in the technology sector, we advise innovative companies, trade associations, investors, and other stakeholders navigating complex regulatory and political environments. Our work sits at the intersection of law, policy, and business, covering key areas such as digital regulation, artificial intelligence, data protection, innovation, financial services, mobility, energy, and health.
Our clients rely on us to
Anticipate and understand policy, regulatory, and institutional developments;
Design and implement effective public affairs and stakeholder engagement strategies;
Build constructive public-private dialogue and help shape policy outcomes;
Navigate legal, governance, and organizational challenges.
With offices in Brussels and Paris, our teams work seamlessly across borders to deliver high-impact advocacy campaigns and strategic advice at the highest levels of decision-making.
Why join us?
Work on some of the most influential EU technology policy files of the moment;
Engage directly with policymakers, regulators, industry leaders, and civil society stakeholders;
Join a collaborative team of experts in digital policy;
Take ownership of client projects and contribute to shaping meaningful regulatory debates;
Develop a unique combination of public affairs, legal, and strategic advisory expertise.
This is an exciting opportunity for a motivated public affairs professional who is passionate about technology, innovation, and European policymaking, and who wants to make a tangible impact on the future of digital regulation in Europe.
Prerequisites
At least 4 years of experience in similar roles;
Team player and can-do attitude;
A deep knowledge of EU institutions and their decision-making processes, gained by interacting with policy makers and regulatory bodies at national and/or EU levels;
Very good understanding of Tech policies and the Brussels Tech ecosystem;
Excellent command of English and good knowledge of French.
Excellent writing skills and ability to translate complex issues suitable for either technical or non-technical audiences and to communicate effectively;
Hands-on experience in project/advocacy campaigns coordination or execution.
How to apply
If you are interested, please send the following by email:
A motivation letter of one page maximum, outlining your motivation for the position and highlighting a key achievement that is particularly relevant to this role;
A detailed CV.
Your complete application should be addressed at
recrutement@cabinet-samman.com
.
Only candidates shortlisted for interview will be contacted. Travel to Paris, in particular in the beginning of the job mission but not only, is required.
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
Share this Job

Policy Advisor (Financial Services)
A&O Shearman
Brussels, Belgium
Job description
Agency applications will not be considered.
A&O Shearman is a new global industry-leading law firm, with nearly 50 offices in 29 countries worldwide. Our fluency in English law, US law, and the laws of the world’s most dynamic markets, enables us to provide unmatched insight and seamless delivery to clients. We work on challenging and important deals and disputes that have the potential to shape the future.
We offer exceptional opportunities for our people; opportunities to work for the world’s leading businesses; to transform the status quo, and to deliver your best work, helping you and your career to thrive, while delivering unparalleled outcomes for our clients.
Whether you're helping clients solve complex challenges, transforming the ways we manage our business, or ensuring the smooth-running of our operations, this is an environment where you can belong and excel. We provide first-rate training and development, we are committed to an inclusive environment, and we provide support and ways of working that help you optimise your wellbeing.
What truly defines a career with us? We recruit the best and ask for the best of you. And together, we will redefine success.
Role purpose
The policy advisor will join A&O Shearman's EU policy task force in Brussels. It acts as the firm's ears and eyes on the ground in Brussels: anticipating regulatory shifts across different sectors and policy areas, cutting through the noise, joining the dots across practices, and turning policy intelligence into practical, client-centric advice. Its work spans policy horizon scanning, internal and client-facing publications, events, training, and tailored client advisory.
The policy advisor will contribute across different policy areas, with a particular focus on financial services, including banking, asset management, digital finance and sustainable finance.
Key relationships
CE head of knowledge;
EU policy manager and EU policy advisor;
Knowledge lawyers;
CE office knowledge heads;
Global knowledge heads;
Head of CE BD;
Head of global library and research;
Campaign and contents team.
What you will do
Policy intelligence and horizon scanning:
You track, analyse and anticipate EU legislative and regulatory developments relevant to our lawyers and clients, with a particular focus on financial services;
You contribute to the Task Force's regular intelligence products, distilling key policy developments, regulatory signals and their strategic implications for the firm and its clients;
You support the A&O Shearman lawyers in providing timely, insightful and forward-looking analysis rather than isolated updates.
Client-facing advisory:
You draft client updates and alerts on regulatory developments, tailored to client sectors or specific topics;
You prepare bespoke policy briefings and intelligence to support client meetings and pitches;
You contribute to client webinars and events;
Training and capability building;
You support internal training for lawyers across the firm's EU and global offices, on various EU policy topics;
You contribute to external training sessions with clients and prospects.
Network building and external engagement:
You proactively build and grow a network around key topics, engaging with policymakers, industry experts, trade associations and clients to stay informed and share insights;
You support the firm's engagement with business associations, including through working groups, and identifying speaking opportunities;
You contribute to the Task Force's external visibility through thought leadership and flagship external products.
Cross-practice and cross-regional collaboration:
You work closely with lawyers across practice groups and regions to help clients anticipate regulatory change and to turn EU policy intelligence into client opportunities across the firm's global network;
You collaborate closely with the business development, knowledge and campaign functions to achieve the firm's strategic goals;
You contribute to the smooth functioning of the firm's EU law community, including its internal knowledge hub, and build up your own knowledge and experience in key topics.
Who we are looking for
You hold a degree or higher in
law, international affairs, public affairs, political science, economics
or related field;
You have at least
3-4 years of relevant professional experience
, preferably within an
EU institution or the EU public affairs
industry;
Experience in EU financial services (such as banking, asset management, digital finance, or sustainable finance) is a strong advantage;
You possess a strong understanding of EU law, policymaking, and the EU legislative process;
You have a
near-native level of English
(additional EU languages are a plus);
You have proven experience drafting clear and concise reports and materials;
You are comfortable leveraging AI tools to support monitoring, analysis, knowledge sharing, and content production;
You are a proactive self-starter with a strong learning mindset and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively;
You have excellent networking, stakeholder management, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to develop trusted relationships internally and externally;
You have a client-centric mindset and can translate complex policy developments into practical advice;
You are a highly effective communicator, both orally and in writing;
You possess strong analytical and problem-solving skills, enabling you to assess competing priorities and develop structured solutions;
You are highly organised and capable of coordinating and delivering projects across multiple teams and stakeholders;
You thrive in a fast-paced, intellectually demanding environment and perform effectively under pressure and tight deadlines;
You demonstrate resilience, professionalism, and the ability to build credibility and trust over time.
What we can offer you
a competitive salary;
flexible benefits via a flex income plan (e.g. extra holidays, bike lease, insurances);
full public transport reimbursement and additional commuting allowances;
a hybrid working model with homeworking allowance and full IT equipment;
meal vouchers of 10€/day;
an iPhone with subscription;
overtime compensation;
extensive learning and development programmes, coaching and language training;
a full insurance package:
comprehensive health coverage including hospitalisation for you and your family;
life, pension, accident and disability insurance;
business travel insurance.
In addition, we offer a work environment designed to support both performance and wellbeing:
We provide a modern, purpose-designed office space, with a mix of collaborative areas and quiet working zones;
We offer technology and infrastructure that support flexible and hybrid working;
We have an in-house café with a barista;
We provide access to a gym and optional personal training;
We organise regular social events and team activities, fostering a strong community culture;
We support flexible and hybrid working arrangements, depending on business needs and team requirements.
Application process
We are committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone can thrive and welcome applications from all eligible candidates.
We invite you to submit your application via the online tool available on our careers website. Please note that applications submitted by email or via an agency will not be considered.
To support your application, kindly upload your CV and cover letter (in English). Only complete application files can be taken into consideration.
As part of our recruitment process, and in order to comply with our legal obligations and internal policies, we require successful candidates to undergo a background screening. The screening also involves providing information on your criminal history through a separate private statement. We will only process information that is necessary and relevant to the position you are applying for. Access to this statement will be strictly limited to the local recruitment officer responsible for your application. Your background screening data will be deleted at the latest six months after receipt. Please see our
data privacy notice
for more details. If you have any questions, feel free to contact
HRBelgium@aoshearman.com
.
Apply Now
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
Share this Job

Contracts Officer
EUMETSAT - European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites
Darmstadt, Germany
Up to € 10,000 per month net
EUMETSAT is Europe’s meteorological satellite agency, operating satellites that monitor the weather and climate from space - 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.
The Contracts Division (COS) is EUMETSAT's centre of expertise for procurement, contractual and commercial matters. Its mission is to ensure that best value for money is achieved through procurements that are compliant, competitive, timely and well managed. The Division is responsible for monitoring the compliant implementation of EUMETSAT's Procurement Procedures and acts as a key partner to all areas of the Organisation throughout the procurement lifecycle.
The Division provides contractual and commercial advice and support, contributes to procurement planning and strategy, participates in evaluations and negotiations, and ensures compliance with EUMETSAT's procurement and financial rules, procedures and quality standards. It negotiates and concludes contracts on behalf of the Organisation and supports the management of contractual matters during contract execution, including amendments, options, performance-related issues, remedies and contract close-out activities.
EUMETSAT's procurements range from contracts valued at approximately EUR 100,000 to multi-million-euro procurements supporting major satellite programmes and operational services. Most procurements are conducted through open competitive tendering procedures and cover a diverse portfolio including launch services, ground segment developments, industrial support services, skills- and product-based service contracts, consultancy services, technical and scientific studies, information technology, general supplies, and site and facility services in support of both EUMETSAT's mandatory and optional programmes.
The Contracts Officer will take contractual responsibility, as part of interdisciplinary procurement and project teams, for the preparation, negotiation and management of contracts and procurements under their assigned responsibility, including competitive tenders and in direct negotiation with single suppliers. The post holder will ensure compliance with EUMETSAT’s contractual, procurement and financial rules, whilst contributing to the achievement of best value for money. The post is currently assigned to the procurement and commercial support of service procurements in the Technical and Scientific Support and Operations and Services departments, supporting a diverse portfolio of operational, technical and engineering activities.
Duties
Preparation of contractual tender documentation;
Review of contractual and technical tender documentation;
Oversight and management of procurement actions, including negotiations;
Management of contractual matters during the execution phase, including contract amendments and options;
Supporting and participating in Tender Evaluation Boards;
Build and maintain trusted and constructive relationships with internal customers, project teams, managers, suppliers and other stakeholders, acting as a trusted procurement partner, and facilitating effective engagement, communication and problem/solving throughout the procurement and contractual lifecycle;
Contribute to the continuous improvement and transformation of EUMETSAT's procurement and contractual processes, tools and working practices, by supporting process optimisation, standardisation, digitalisation and organisational change initiatives, aimed at enhancing efficiency, compliance and quality;
Preparation and negotiation of co-operation agreements with national and international partners;
People management tasks.
Employment conditions
Excellent salary, of up to Euro 10,000/month
NET (after income tax)
based on skills and experience;
Flexible working time including additional flexi-leave;
Full medical coverage for employee and family;
Attractive pension;
30 days annual leave + 14.5 days public holidays;
Training and development support;
Relocation allowance (if applicable).
Skills and experience
Demonstrated experience (typically at least 5-10 years) in the procurement of supplies and/or complex services, especially through competitive public tendering, and negotiation and commercial management of contracts, for complex high technology systems, in a satellite, aerospace, or engineering environment and preferably gained in the frame of international or national public procurement;
Proven experience in independently drafting and negotiating contract terms and conditions, legal provisions and dealing with contractual matters, and the ability to understand complex technical and legal issues and to formulate clear legal texts;
Excellent stakeholder management, communication and influencing skills, with the demonstrated ability to build consensus, foster collaboration, develop and sustain positive working relationships with a diverse range of technical, operational and managerial stakeholders within multidisciplinary teams, resolving issues through constructive engagement, sound judgement and effective communication;
